@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il29-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il29-time`
IMPORT `ito-il29-published-figures`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance s 2(2)(b) and the Income Tax (Value of Use of a Mobile Radio Telephone) Regulations,
-- 5762-2002 (TEL): the monthly value of the use of a mobile telephone put at an employee's disposal.
-- Row IL-29.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `The monthly value of the use of a mobile telephone`

-- src:TEL:16 | ”הוצאה חודשית“ – הוצאות שהוצאו בחודש בשל רדיו טלפון נייד, לרבות הוצאות קבועות;
-- src:TEL:17 | ”הועמד לרשות העובד“ – ניתן לשימושו האישי של העובד.
-- src:TEL:20 | שווי השימוש לכל חודש ברדיו טלפון נייד שהועמד לרשות העובד, למעט רדיו טלפון כאמור שניתן להתקשר ממנו למקום העבודה בלבד, יהיה מחצית מההוצאה החודשית, או 80 שקלים חדשים [note: (מתואם לשנת 2002; בשנים 2019 עד 2022, 105 ש״ח; בשנים 2023 עד 2027, 115 ש״ח)] לפי הנמוך, והכל בניכוי סכום ההוצאה החודשית ששילם העובד בשל אותו רדיו טלפון נייד.

@ref TEL reg 2, line 20: a telephone from which only the workplace can be called
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Regulations fix no value for a telephone from which calls can be made to the place of work only` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Regulations fix no value for a mobile telephone from which calls can be made to the place of work only, and s 2(2)(b) fixes none otherwise: the text does not say what its use is worth"

@ref TEL reg 1, line 16 ("הוצאה חודשית"): the employee cannot have paid more than the expense
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the employee's payment exceeds the monthly expense` MEANS
    REFUSE "the part of the monthly expense the employee paid is negative or exceeds the monthly expense"

@ref TEL reg 2, line 20; fork XD
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      p IS A `A mobile telephone put at an employee's disposal`
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the monthly values of the use of a mobile telephone, on the readings allowed, in the tax year` y `, of` p `under` r MEANS
    IF   p's `a telephone from which calls can be made to the place of work only`
    THEN `the Regulations fix no value for a telephone from which calls can be made to the place of work only`
    ELSE IF   p's `the part of the monthly expense the employee paid` LESS THAN 0
              OR p's `the part of the monthly expense the employee paid` GREATER THAN p's `the monthly expense`
         THEN `the employee's payment exceeds the monthly expense`
         ELSE `the values of a result of`
                  ((min ((p's `the monthly expense`) DIVIDED BY 2) (`the ceiling of the monthly value of use of a mobile telephone, as published, in the tax year` y))
                   MINUS p's `the part of the monthly expense the employee paid`)
                  `when a deduction may exceed the value, read` (r's `excess deduction`)

@ref TEL reg 2, line 20
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the monthly value of the use of the telephone is not settled by the readings allowed` MEANS
    REFUSE "the monthly value of the use of the telephone is not settled: the Regulations do not say what the value is where the employee paid more than the value (nil, or negative)"

@export The monthly value of the use of a mobile telephone put at an employee's disposal under Income Tax Ordinance s 2(2)(b) and the Regulations of 5762-2002, for a tax year from 2024: the lower of half the monthly expense and the ceiling (NIS 115 for 2023 to 2027), less what the employee paid of the expense; declines where that is below zero, as the text does not say what it is then
@ref ITO s 2(2)(b), lines 217-220; TEL reg 2, line 20
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
          @desc the tax year, from 2024 to 2027 (the ceiling is published for those years)
      p IS A `A mobile telephone put at an employee's disposal`
          @desc whether only the workplace can be called from it, the monthly expense, and the part of it the employee paid
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2(2)(b) — the monthly value of the use of a mobile telephone in the tax year` y `, of` p `under` r MEANS
    `for` (`the calendar tax year` y) `, row IL-29 answers`
        (`the single number among`
            (`the monthly values of the use of a mobile telephone, on the readings allowed, in the tax year` y `, of` p `under` r) `, else`
            (`the monthly value of the use of the telephone is not settled by the readings allowed`))

§ `The value for a tax year`

-- The Regulations fix a value "לכל חודש" (for each month).  How a part of a month is treated is not said (fork PM).
@ref ITO s 2(2)(b); VEH reg 2(a), line 36; TEL reg 2, line 20: fork PM
GIVEN u  IS A `The use of a vehicle in a tax year`
      rd IS A `A reading of a part of a month`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the months of use to count, given` u `, read` rd MEANS
    IF   u's `days of a further part of a month` EQUALS 0
    THEN LIST (u's `whole months it was at the employee's disposal`)
    ELSE CONSIDER rd
         WHEN `declined where the readings differ` THEN LIST (whole PLUS 1), (whole PLUS fraction), whole
         WHEN `a part of a month counts as a month` THEN LIST (whole PLUS 1)
         WHEN `a part of a month is prorated by days` THEN LIST (whole PLUS fraction)
         WHEN `a part of a month does not count` THEN LIST whole
    WHERE
        whole    MEANS u's `whole months it was at the employee's disposal`
        fraction MEANS (u's `days of a further part of a month`) DIVIDED BY (u's `days in that month`)

@ref ITO s 2(2)(b): the months given
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the months of use given are negative, over twelve, or the part month does not fit its month` MEANS
    REFUSE "the months of use given are negative or over twelve, or the days of the further part of a month are negative or not fewer than the days in that month"

@export The value for a tax year of the use of a vehicle or a mobile telephone, from its monthly value and the months it was at the employee's disposal; a part of a month is a fork and declines by default
@ref ITO s 2(2)(b); fork PM
GIVEN monthly IS A NUMBER
      u       IS A `The use of a vehicle in a tax year`
      r       IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the value for the tax year, from the monthly value` monthly `, for` u `, under` r MEANS
    IF   u's `whole months it was at the employee's disposal` LESS THAN 0
         OR u's `days of a further part of a month` LESS THAN 0
         OR u's `days of a further part of a month` AT LEAST u's `days in that month`
         OR (u's `whole months it was at the employee's disposal`) PLUS (IF u's `days of a further part of a month` GREATER THAN 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0) GREATER THAN 12
    THEN `the months of use given are negative, over twelve, or the part month does not fit its month`
    ELSE `the single number among`
             (map (GIVEN months YIELD monthly TIMES months) (`the months of use to count, given` u `, read` (r's `part month`)))
             `, else` `the months to count are not settled by the readings allowed`

@ref ITO s 2(2)(b); fork PM
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the months to count are not settled by the readings allowed` MEANS
    REFUSE "the months to count are not settled: the Regulations fix a value for each month and do not say whether a part of a month counts as a month, is prorated by days, or does not count"
